  "applies_to": "ONICON F-1500 series insertion turbine flow meters with the communication type set to BACnet MS/TP.",
  "summary": "The F-1500 turbine meter can run BACnet MS/TP on its RS-485 port. It exposes 19 Analog Inputs (volume, mass and energy flow, two temperatures, pressure, density, two totalizers, output channel values, velocity and turbine diagnostics), three alarm Binary Inputs, an external-input BI and a totalizer-reset BV.",
  "bacnet_transport": [
    "BACnet MS/TP"
  ],
  "firmware": "Application software 1.07",
  "default_device_instance": 7,
  "access_inferred": false,
  "notes": [
    "Which values carry data depends on the meter build and configuration; several objects are marked 'TBD' in the manual's description column.",
    "Units follow the meter's configured display units. The manual prints rate units for the totalizers; the totalizer unit depends on whether it counts mass, volume or energy.",
    "AI 8 and AI 9 are printed as one row ('Totalizer 1 & Totalizer 2'); the PICS lists them separately as AI 8 and AI 9.",
    "Present_Value and Out_Of_Service are listed as writable for AI, BI and BV; writing an input's Present_Value only makes sense with Out_Of_Service set.",
    "BI 4 always reads 0.",
    "Source: F-1500 manual DOC-0003872, section 4.3 (PICS dated 19-April-2012)."
  ],
  "source": {
    "title": "F-1500 Insertion Turbine Flow Meter Installation and Operation Manual",
